## PARALLEL-SESSION COORDINATION — wq leases + slock (2026-07-11) #CORE
Overlap fix (Frank directive): agents were duplicating work because coordination was prose.
Now enforced in tooling — full rules in instructions/playbooks/session-start.md §PARALLEL-SESSION
COORDINATION. Summary: (1) ALL agent work is a `wq` ticket claimed via atomic `wq claim`
(user lane refuses claims); claims carry a 240m lease that auto-expires back to open —
`wq heartbeat <id>` extends; `wq add` refuses duplicate normalized titles. (2) Before
state-changing work on any shared subsystem, `slock acquire <scope> --holder <session-name>`
(auto-expiring advisory lock on queue.db; DENIED = hands off). (3) Use a stable session name
for wq agent + slock holder. HANDOFF prose ownership ("wq#N owned by session X") is retired —
if it's not a claimed ticket or a held slock, nobody owns it. Backups: wq.bak.20260712_024158,
queue.db.bak.20260712_024158. Shipped session claude-fable-coord 2026-07-11.

